    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP is defined by a singular, frustrating bottleneck: almost our entire high-speed core\u2014led by **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, and the speed-threat prospect **Travis Bazzana**\u2014is sidelined by the current schedule rotation. With those anchors unavailable, we are forced to lean on **Brice Turang** as our primary engine. **Brice Turang** holds a marginal 45.17 score against Rasmussen; while the SP_xERA of 3.30 is a limiting factor, the 3% boost from the platoon advantage and his spot in the #5 hole keeps him in the daily mix. We are effectively operating in \"preservation mode\" today, as the absence of **James Wood** and **Corbin Carroll** means we are sacrificing our stolen base floor to manage our remaining game caps efficiently.\n\nThe internal debate regarding today\u2019s utility spots centered on the depth of the infield and the recent surge from **Mickey Moniak**. While **Mickey Moniak** was knocking on the door of the \"Strong\" (60+) threshold, he narrowly missed the starting cut due to the organizational mandate to prioritize the OBP/SLG profile of **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** in better park factors. **Isaac Paredes** and **Max Muncy** remain on the bench as well, as their current efficiency scores failed to overcome the friction of today\u2019s pitcher matchups. We continue to monitor the status of **Trevor Story** and **Seiya Suzuki**; if the wind shifts favorably in their respective ballparks, we may look to swap them in, but for now, we are comfortable keeping **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Moises Ballesteros**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young** in a developmental stasis. Today is about maintaining roster health while waiting for the speed profiles of **Jose Caballero** and the rest of the vanguard to return to action.",
